    "text": "Let f be a continuous function satisfying&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>dx</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;. Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
